From the air, the scale of the flooding across Southwest Colorado is striking.

@SenatorBennet and I departed Alamosa aboard a Black Hawk helicopter to survey flood damage in Archuleta and La Plata counties. Washed-out roads and damaged infrastructure have left families and businesses facing another difficult recovery, with many communities still rebuilding from last year’s storms.

Grateful to the flight crews, first responders, and local officials working on the ground. Seeing the damage firsthand reinforces the urgency of securing federal resources to restore essential services and help these communities rebuild. #CO03
